{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7LfMJukvn6HSu7af5C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For [Ni(NH₃)₆]²⁺ the three bands fit best at **Dq ≈ 1085 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 824 cm⁻¹**. That gives 10Dq ≈ 10 850 cm⁻¹ and C = 4.5B ≈ 3710 cm⁻¹. C is only an assumption here, because these bands do not depend on it.\n\n**Model**\n\nOctahedral d⁸ has the ³A₂g ground state. Only the triplet terms matter for these spin-allowed bands, and their energies (in cm⁻¹, relative to the ground state) are:\n\n- ν₁ = ³A₂ → ³T₂ = 10Dq\n- ν₂ and ν₃ (³A₂ → ³T₁ and ³T₁(2)) = 7.5B + 15Dq ∓ ½√(225B² − 180B·Dq + 100Dq²)\n\nC does not enter any of these, so it cannot be determined from the bands.\n\n**The simple closed-form route does not agree with itself**\n\n- From ν₁ alone, Dq = 1060.\n- The sum ν₂ + ν₃ = 15B + 30Dq then gives B ≈ 887.\n- Solving ν₂ alone with Dq = 1060 gives B ≈ 1077.\n- Solving ν₃ alone with Dq = 1060 gives B ≈ 851.\n\nThese three B values disagree, so the three bands cannot be matched exactly with one pair of parameters. The usual reasons are that a spin-forbidden ¹E level sits near ³T₁ and mixes with it, and that real band maxima are not exactly the pure-term energies.\n\n**Least-squares fit to all three bands**\n\nI fitted all three bands at once with the fitting tool. I passed C = 3990 cm⁻¹ to it, but the tool confirmed the fitted levels do not depend on C, so the result also holds for C/B = 4.5.\n\n| Band | Observed (cm⁻¹) | Calculated (cm⁻¹) | Residual (cm⁻¹) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ³T₂ | 10 600 | 10 846 | +246 |\n| ³T₁ | 17 500 | 17 216 | −284 |\n| ³T₁(2) | 27 600 | 27 680 | +80 |\n\nThe root-mean-square error is about 220 cm⁻¹, which is fine for broad Ni(II) bands.\n\nB ≈ 824 cm⁻¹ is about 76 % of the free Ni²⁺ value (about 1080 cm⁻¹, a standard tabulated value; I did not run the covalency tool to check it). That modest reduction is typical for ammine ligands.\n\nIf you instead fix Dq from ν₁ alone (1060 cm⁻¹), the sum rule gives B ≈ 887 cm⁻¹.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1085, \"B\": 824, \"C\": 3707, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Least-squares fit of the three spin-allowed d8 bands; C taken as 4.5B because the triplet bands do not depend on C.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1343,"cache_read_input_tokens":8036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1343,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dfeb1e17-dac6-4015-9804-618203687493","uuid":"c32e6644-d517-4e50-82ed-ed614206c8f0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:37:02.628Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7Lf2TgyUHmWinN6V4y"}
